---
description: NestJS/backend conventions for apps/api and libs/backend
globs: apps/api/**/*.ts,libs/backend/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# NestJS conventions

- Validate every request body with a `class-validator` DTO. The global
  `ValidationPipe` uses `whitelist: true` but **not** `transform: true` — so
  numeric/date fields must already be the right type (use `@Type(() => Date)`
  from `class-transformer` for dates); don't rely on implicit string→number
  coercion.
- Protect admin-only routes with `@Roles('ADMIN')` +
  `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)` (see
  `libs/backend/orders/src/lib/order.controller.ts`).
- Money is always an integer in minor currency units, never a float — see
  `Dish.basicPrice`'s doc comment in `prisma/schema.prisma`.
- Read-then-write on a shared row (tokens, seat availability, stock) is a race
  condition waiting to happen — use an atomic `updateMany` with the
  precondition in the `WHERE` clause instead (see `AuthService.refresh()`).
- New backend features live in their own `libs/backend/<name>` lib (module +
  controller + service + dto), wired into `apps/api/src/app/app.module.ts`.
